<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81142" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί-βλεπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>looked at from all sides,
				admired of all observers</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					89
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταὧς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					175.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					10.1
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν φύσιν τινὸς ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					10.17
				</span></i>
			; mostly of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. βροτοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					508
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Pr.</u>
				31.23
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντων . . -ότατοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					7.1.30
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ ταῦτα π. εἶναι ἐν Ἕλλησι καὶ
					ἐν βαρβάροις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					8.38
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. παρά τισι</span> Carneïsc.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1027.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				13.92
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐπ᾽ ἀρετῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					8.141
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.48
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ πάντων ἐπὶ κακίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.95
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρσάκης</span>
			 (
				Sup.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>; freq. as a title of honour, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1038.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>, etc. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἀγωνίσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					18.30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
